      <p><strong>Multi-location booking software, also called multi-branch or multi-site booking software, runs bookings, staff and payments for several locations in one system. It gives every site the same calendar, lets staff move between locations and shows the owner every branch at once. Zennly is built for this.</strong></p>

      <h2>Why a second location breaks the old way</h2>
      <p>With one site, a notebook or spreadsheet works. With two, locations promise the same staff member, prices and discounts drift, and nobody can say what each site earned yesterday without phoning managers. Multi-location software puts every site on one calendar and one set of records.</p>

      <h2>Features worth looking for</h2>
      <p>These are the features that decide whether the software copes with growth:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>One booking calendar across locations, with clashes refused</li>
        <li>Staff transfers scheduled in advance, with an effective date</li>
        <li>One service menu and price list, with differences only where you choose</li>
        <li>Discount requests approved by a manager and recorded with an audit trail</li>
        <li>Payments recorded by method at the point of service, and a daily close per location</li>
        <li>Role-based access for owners, managers and front desk</li>
        <li>Reports and a dashboard that compare every location</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Names for the same thing</h2>
      <p>The USA and Canada usually say 'multi-location', while the UK, Australia, the UAE and Nepal also say 'multi-branch' or 'multi-site'. The software is the same, so search for whichever word you use.</p>

      <h2>Who needs it</h2>
      <p>Any appointment-based business with more than one site: spas, salons and beauty parlours, gyms and personal trainers, physiotherapy clinics, tattoo studios and cleaning companies. If you plan a second site, choose software that already handles several.</p>

      <h2>Common mistakes with several locations</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Running a separate calendar tool at each site, so staff and bookings cannot be compared</li>
        <li>Copying price lists by hand, so prices drift between locations</li>
        <li>Moving staff between sites by message instead of a scheduled transfer</li>
        <li>Closing the day differently at each site, so totals cannot be compared</li>
        <li>Giving every user full access instead of limiting what each role can see</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The common thread is that each site works alone. One shared system removes most of these at once.</p>

      <h2>Questions to ask before you buy</h2>
      <p>Ask how pricing changes when you add a location, whether staff can work at more than one site, how discounts are controlled, how each location closes the day, and what the owner sees. Ask for a demo with your own locations and services.</p>

      <h2>Where Zennly fits</h2>
      <p>Zennly is built for multi-location businesses, with one calendar, staff transfers, discount approval, payment tracking, a daily close and reports for every location. See the <a href="/features/booking/">booking</a>, <a href="/features/staff-management/">staff</a> and <a href="/features/payment-tracking/">payment</a> features, or the <a href="/case-study/">four-branch case study</a>. Zennly can be set up for businesses in any country on request.</p>

      <h2>Common questions</h2>
      <h3>What is multi-location booking software?</h3>
      <p>It is software that runs bookings, staff and payments for several locations in one system, so every site shares one calendar and the owner sees all of them together.</p>
      <h3>Is multi-location the same as multi-branch booking software?</h3>
      <p>Yes. Multi-location is the common term in the USA and Canada. Multi-branch and multi-site are common in the UK, Australia, the UAE and Nepal.</p>
      <h3>When does a business need multi-location software?</h3>
      <p>When you have, or plan, a second site, and staff, prices or discounts start to drift between locations.</p>

